                <pb facs="0797" n="699" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg699"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Everett to Mr.
                            Bonilla</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-11-06"><hi rendition="#italic">November 6,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Your excellency’s telegram received informing me that Government of Honduras had
                    decided to pay the indemnity demanded in the Pears case and that drafts for
                    required amount would be sent me immediately. I shall acknowledge their receipt
                    as soon as received.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Everett</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Chargé d’Affaires.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
